  {"tool":"create_page","arguments":{"page":"README","text":"# Space Shooter\n\nA side-scrolling shooter: hold off the aliens streaming in from the right for as long as you can.\n\n## Words\n\n- **Ship**: the player's ship ([Ship](../src/commonMain/kotlin/actors/Ship.kt))\n- **Laser**: a shot the ship fires ([Laser](../src/commonMain/kotlin/actors/Laser.kt))\n- **Alien**: an enemy ([Alien](../src/commonMain/kotlin/actors/Alien.kt))\n- **Sparks**: the bits an alien bursts into ([Spark](../src/commonMain/kotlin/actors/Spark.kt))\n- **Stars**: the starfield behind it all ([Star](../src/commonMain/kotlin/actors/Star.kt))\n- **Score**: points, kept by [Game](../src/commonMain/kotlin/managers/Game.kt)\n\n## How it plays\n\nThe ship sits near the left edge of [space](../src/commonMain/composeResources/files/scenes/space.json) and flies up and down with the Up and Down arrows (or W and S), never leaving the screen. Space fires a laser straight to the right.\n\nEvery second or so an alien flies in from the right edge at a random height and speed, drifting slightly up or down. A laser that hits an alien destroys both, and the alien bursts into a shower of orange sparks that fade away. Each alien destroyed is worth 10 points, shown in the top left corner.\n\nIf an alien touches the ship, space starts over and the score goes back to 0. Aliens that slip past the left edge are gone.\n\nStars of different sizes and brightness scroll leftwards at different speeds, so the nearer ones seem to rush by and the far ones to crawl.\n"}},
  {"tool":"edit_page","arguments":{"page":"README","section":"Words","text":"## Words\n\n- **Ship**: the player's ship (the Ship Actor type)\n- **Laser**: a shot the ship fires (Laser)\n- **Alien**: an enemy (Alien)\n- **Sparks**: the bits an alien bursts into (Spark)\n- **Stars**: the starfield behind it all (Star)\n- **Score**: points, kept by the Game Manager type\n"}}
